Hmm.  Most odd.  I've never done a make boot before.

I've got 2.2.19 running on an x86 platform at home.  It acts as our
fileserver, and internet gateway.  Anyways.  I always do:

cd /usr/src/linux

make xconfig
make dep
make clean
make bzImage
make modules
make modules_install

Then I copy the bzImage and System.map to /boot:

cp arch/i386/boot/bzImage /boot
cp System.map /boot

Then I re-edit/re-run lilo.

And things have always worked fine.  So fine, in fact, I do most of my
kernel updates remotely from home, so's not to disturb folks in the office
during business hours.-
Chris


