I was wondering if anyone has managed to boot an Alpha-Linux with the 
roots filesystem placed in a volume group (LVM).

I have a system with AlphaBIOS+MILO, and I have come as far as to get 
the kernel to load an initrd, and execute the linuxrc, which 
successfully activates the VGs. The contents of 
'/proc/sys/kernel/real-root-dev', doesn't seem to get things right, and 
cat'ing the appropriate devno into said file, doesn't seem to make 
things any better.

I know of one method, which I am reluctant to use, namely to mount a 
filesystem, which contains an /etc/fstab in which the rootfs is listed
as the VG, thus leaving it to the init(8) system initialization to take 
care of switching - but that way I'll never get my rootfs fsck'd during 
boot.

