Hi,
This is a basic problem i also have.
Originally the 2100 have the Compaq Qvision Eisa card as graphics. This is
the basic configuration and the SRM knows this card, because it is added
automatically when you run the EISA utility. The needed config file is on
the diskette and loaded automatically. For any card, including graphics, you
need this hardware-specific config file to let SRM know what is in the box.
Only those cards added with the EISA configuration utility will be seen by
SRM and pitty enough both Tru64 and Linux run via SRM. Installing any of
them without the card beeing seen by SRM will install in textmode, without
CDE, because there is no X-server and there will never be as long as SRM
does not report a graphic card upon installation.
NT and W2K have no problem and accept any card, be it ISA, EISA, or PCI,
because they use the ARC console.
Sad enough, even with Tru64 running good with the Qvision, Linux has no
driver for it and can only be installed in textmode.
I hope i am wrong with this last statement and some specialist corrects me
and with that also soves my problem with Linux and Qvision.

Harry
