The problem with Netscape's browser on Alpha is it dumps core
(segmentation faults, IIRC) whenever it feels like it, and that's
pretty often.  Redhat's home page used to cause it with perfect
repeatability.  Turning off Javascript and Java keep the browser
up, but that makes the browser useless for many sites/pages.

Mozilla works, more or less.  If we're lucky, it has advanced
since I last tested it to the point where the "save source as"
function actually allows the user to type in the name of a file
that does not already exist.  However, on those same pages that
cause Netscape to dump core, the version of Mozilla that comes
with RH7.1 tries to download and install an X86 Java runtime
environment.  Wrong answer, try again!

