Well, to do a little defending on Digital's behalf....

The PWSxxx-a series of systems were designed and qualified to run AlphaNT only.
The configurations shipped would sucessfully boot from AlphaBIOS. No other
operating system or SRM was supported.

The PWSxxx-au series were designed to run OpenVMS and Tru64 Unix and were
shipped with hardware that SRM understood.

It is possible to install SRM on a PWSxxx-a (my PWS500a boots from SRM) and
as it has had a SCSI controller upgrade can be booted from SRM. I suspect
(but haven't tested) that my PWS500-a might well boot OpenVMS, not that I
really need another VMS box right now....
